WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.978 --> 00:00:18.823
A few minutes later, the kids were in the main room facing the adults.

2
00:00:19.623 --> 00:00:21.084
Venna glared at the stowaways.

3
00:00:21.104 --> 00:00:22.925
"This is outrageous!

4
00:00:23.365 --> 00:00:25.706
The expedition is supposed to be top secret."

5
00:00:25.726 --> 00:00:28.307
"Does that mean we have to turn back?"

6
00:00:28.707 --> 00:00:30.208
Gliss sounded almost hopeful.

7
00:00:31.056 --> 00:00:36.098
"If so, the furies will have to rest for a few days before departing again," Tok warned.

8
00:00:36.118 --> 00:00:38.599
"Impossible." Venna frowned.

9
00:00:38.619 --> 00:00:42.061
"The king and queen won't appreciate any delay.

10
00:00:42.741 --> 00:00:44.802
Besides, there's no need to turn back.

11
00:00:45.582 --> 00:00:47.663
These kids can zap themselves home.

12
00:00:48.023 --> 00:00:51.044
We aren't close enough to the Cave yet to interfere with their magic."

13
00:00:51.865 --> 00:00:53.645
"No zapping," Tok said.

14
00:00:53.965 --> 00:00:56.126
"The furies will sense that level of magic.

15
00:00:56.827 --> 00:00:58.427
They'll get distracted and crash."

16
00:00:59.268 --> 00:01:00.048
Zann gulped.

17
00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.002
Tok had warned them earlier about not using any major magic during the journey.

18
00:01:05.442 --> 00:01:06.582
Now he understood why.

19
00:01:06.602 --> 00:01:09.784
"Perda and Darb will have to come with us then."

20
00:01:10.504 --> 00:01:11.704
Teplo glanced at Tok.

21
00:01:11.724 --> 00:01:14.045
"Is it safe to summon a message moth?

22
00:01:14.685 --> 00:01:16.606
We should let their parents know they're with us."

23
00:01:17.407 --> 00:01:21.388
"Yes, that minor sort of magic should be okay," Tok said.

24
00:01:21.408 --> 00:01:23.689
"We can't use magic?"

25
00:01:24.029 --> 00:01:25.070
Perda whispered to Zann.

26
00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:27.671
"It's like Morb is back again!"

27
00:01:27.691 --> 00:01:29.731
"Don't say that."

28
00:01:30.212 --> 00:01:30.832
Zann shuddered.

29
00:01:31.668 --> 00:01:33.329
"Let's explore the rest of the ship."

30
00:01:38.173 --> 00:01:38.813
for landing!"

31
00:01:39.113 --> 00:01:39.894
Tok called out.

32
00:01:40.654 --> 00:01:41.795
Zann peered out the window.

33
00:01:42.175 --> 00:01:45.998
It was the next morning, and the sky was streaked with the remnants of sunrise.

34
00:01:47.099 --> 00:01:50.821
Below lay a vast desert littered with rocks and blowing red sand.

35
00:01:51.642 --> 00:01:56.225
Swirls of energy spurted out of a jagged opening, which looked like a mouth full of teeth.

36
00:01:56.245 --> 00:02:00.028
"The Cave of the Unknown," Zann whispered.

37
00:02:01.128 --> 00:02:05.170
After hearing his parents talk about the place all his life, he was really here!

38
00:02:09.052 --> 00:02:14.636
As the group exited the aircraft, Tok warned everyone not to use magic in or around the Cave.

39
00:02:14.656 --> 00:02:16.797
"We've got something to help you.

40
00:02:17.257 --> 00:02:18.097
I'll fetch it now."

41
00:02:18.117 --> 00:02:20.539
"This place is amazing!"

42
00:02:20.879 --> 00:02:23.540
Perda said, staring at the cave opening in front of them.

43
00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:27.663
"Maybe we'll see some of the famous relics we learned about in school.

44
00:02:28.423 --> 00:02:32.174
Like the Mask of Zanta, or even the Horn of the Otherworld."

45
00:02:33.215 --> 00:02:33.996
Gliss shivered.

46
00:02:34.016 --> 00:02:35.618
"I'm not going in there.

47
00:02:36.298 --> 00:02:37.620
What if we get lost?

48
00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.723
We won't be able to use magic to find our way out."

49
00:02:41.484 --> 00:02:42.224
Teplo heard her.

50
00:02:42.244 --> 00:02:45.268
"Don't worry, that's what cave crawlers are for."

51
00:02:45.288 --> 00:02:47.129
"Cave crawlers?"

52
00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:48.251
Perda echoed.

53
00:02:48.271 --> 00:02:50.233
"Yes. Here they are."

54
00:02:50.673 --> 00:02:53.176
Tok had just returned, carrying a wire cage.

55
00:02:54.072 --> 00:03:00.134
Inside were a dozen large rodents with pale fur, long tails, and huge, glowing eyes.

56
00:03:00.154 --> 00:03:02.715
"Yuck!" Gliss said.

57
00:03:02.735 --> 00:03:05.055
"They look like swamp rats!"

58
00:03:05.075 --> 00:03:07.716
"You'll each get one," Tok said.

59
00:03:07.736 --> 00:03:12.377
"They're native to this area, so they know how to avoid the Cave's energy bursts.

60
00:03:13.277 --> 00:03:17.419
The glowworms they eat give their bodies a natural glow you can use as a light.

61
00:03:18.159 --> 00:03:22.440
And no matter how lost you get, your crawler can find the way out of the Cave."

62
00:03:23.244 --> 00:03:24.305
He set down the cage.

63
00:03:25.066 --> 00:03:27.127
Zing lunged toward it, shooting flames.

64
00:03:27.147 --> 00:03:29.910
"Zing, no!"

65
00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:31.851
said Zann, grabbing the dragon.

66
00:03:32.572 --> 00:03:33.293
He looked at Tok.

67
00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:36.095
"Sorry, I guess he thinks they're food.

68
00:03:36.996 --> 00:03:38.217
I hope he didn't scare them."

69
00:03:38.998 --> 00:03:42.901
"Once your crawler bonds to you, nothing will scare it off," Tok said.

70
00:03:42.921 --> 00:03:46.824
"Be careful not to let Zing actually catch one though."

71
00:03:47.505 --> 00:03:50.868
Tok placed a crawler on Zann's shoulder and muttered a quick spell.

72
00:03:51.644 --> 00:03:55.027
Even that little bit of magic made the energy storms intensify.

73
00:03:55.047 --> 00:03:57.949
"There," said Tok.

74
00:03:57.969 --> 00:04:00.191
"This crawler is bonded to you now."

75
00:04:00.891 --> 00:04:06.636
The crawler dug its claws into Zann's shoulder and chirped nervously at Zing, who was watching it intently.

76
00:04:07.456 --> 00:04:10.639
Meanwhile Tok bonded crawlers to each of the other members of the group.

77
00:04:10.659 --> 00:04:13.801
"All right, everyone," Venna called out.

78
00:04:13.821 --> 00:04:17.584
"We'll begin by locating and cataloging each relic.

79
00:04:18.336 --> 00:04:23.958
I've drawn a diagram of the Cave based on the ancient texts and divided it into several sections."

80
00:04:25.078 --> 00:04:27.759
Venna continued to talk, but Zann stopped listening.

81
00:04:27.779 --> 00:04:34.901
"How can she make something as exciting as exploring the Cave of the Unknown sound so boring?"

82
00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.401
he whispered to his friends.

83
00:04:37.201 --> 00:04:39.882
He wondered what his parents' last journey to the Cave had been like.

84
00:04:40.642 --> 00:04:43.163
He stuck his hand into his pocket and touched the stone.

85
00:04:43.963 --> 00:04:45.603
To his surprise, it felt warm.

86
00:04:45.624 --> 00:04:47.164
"Weird," he muttered.

87
00:04:48.168 --> 00:04:49.469
"What?" Perda asked.

88
00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:54.574
"Nothing." Zann shivered as he took a step toward the gaping cave mouth.

89
00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:55.795
"Let's go in."

90
00:04:59.118 --> 00:05:01.420
The kids spent the next hour exploring the Cave.

91
00:05:02.261 --> 00:05:04.462
Sounds echoed off the cold rock walls.

92
00:05:05.223 --> 00:05:08.066
Tiny, strange creatures scurried through the shadows.

93
00:05:09.207 --> 00:05:12.610
"Oops!" Perda blurted out as they crossed a large, shadowy chamber.

94
00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.231
"What's wrong?"

95
00:05:14.611 --> 00:05:15.152
Zann asked.

96
00:05:16.008 --> 00:05:18.090
"I tripped over a rock or something."

97
00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:19.350
Perda leaned down.

98
00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:22.373
"Actually, it looks like another relic."

99
00:05:23.153 --> 00:05:24.194
Gliss gasped.

100
00:05:24.634 --> 00:05:25.935
"Not just any relic.

101
00:05:26.736 --> 00:05:28.617
I think it's the Horn of the Otherworld!"

102
00:05:28.637 --> 00:05:30.778
"Careful!" Darb said.

103
00:05:30.798 --> 00:05:32.760
"Don't touch—whoa!"

104
00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:35.461
He skidded on some loose stones and fell.

105
00:05:35.482 --> 00:05:37.563
"Darb! Are you okay?"

106
00:05:37.883 --> 00:05:38.504
Gliss cried.

107
00:05:38.524 --> 00:05:41.446
"Sure. I just skinned my knee."

108
00:05:42.186 --> 00:05:43.007
Gliss hurried over.

109
00:05:43.027 --> 00:05:44.768
"Let me see."

110
00:05:45.428 --> 00:05:47.269
She rubbed her fingers to do a Healing spell.

111
00:05:48.069 --> 00:05:49.050
"No magic!"

112
00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:50.050
Zann shouted.

113
00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:51.150
It was too late.

114
00:05:51.711 --> 00:05:54.772
Energy crackled from Gliss' fingertips, and the Horn lit up.

115
00:05:55.592 --> 00:05:57.033
Zann felt the air sizzle.

116
00:05:57.433 --> 00:06:00.254
Zap! "Ow!"

117
00:06:00.654 --> 00:06:03.115
he exclaimed, landing hard in a different tunnel.

118
00:06:03.716 --> 00:06:05.897
A second later his friends landed beside him.

119
00:06:05.917 --> 00:06:07.517
"What happened?"

120
00:06:07.817 --> 00:06:08.378
Gliss cried.

121
00:06:08.398 --> 00:06:11.479
"You used magic," Perda said.

122
00:06:11.499 --> 00:06:13.900
"The Horn must have zapped us away!"

123
00:06:15.008 --> 00:06:15.948
"Where are we?"

124
00:06:16.269 --> 00:06:17.409
Gliss sounded panicky.

125
00:06:17.429 --> 00:06:19.730
"Don't worry," Darb said.

126
00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:21.751
"Our crawlers can find the way out."

127
00:06:22.811 --> 00:06:23.772
Zann cocked his head.

128
00:06:23.792 --> 00:06:25.552
"Maybe they won't have to.

129
00:06:26.353 --> 00:06:27.413
I hear someone talking.

130
00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:29.394
We must have landed near the entrance."

131
00:06:30.154 --> 00:06:31.635
He hurried in the direction of the voice.

132
00:06:32.435 --> 00:06:33.876
It was coming from the next chamber.

133
00:06:33.896 --> 00:06:36.957
"Hello," Zann called as he entered the chamber.

134
00:06:36.977 --> 00:06:40.899
"We—" Zann took one look at the speaker and gasped.

135
00:06:41.979 --> 00:06:42.199
It was
